{"type": "final", "turn": 3, "content": "\n\nShort answer: none. With these 300 random labels, **no part of the map certifies to a \u2264 5% error rate** (alpha = 0.05, delta = 0.1) \u2014 under either the prefix or Bonferroni rule, every candidate zone was rejected.\n\n| Zone (most-confident windows) | Labels inside | Wrong | One-sided upper bound |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| top 15% (~2,372 windows) | 46 | 3 | ~13.9% |\n| top 25% (~3,953) | 68 | 3 | ~9.5% |\n| top 50% (~7,906) | 140 | 13 | ~13.2% |\n| whole map (15,813) | 300 | 69 | ~26.4% |\n\nEven the most confident 15% of the map only reaches a ~14% worst-case error bound \u2014 the observed 3/46 errors inside it are too few for the exact test to push the bound under 5%. Nothing outside any tested zone is certified either.\n\nTo get a certified zone you'd need either (a) substantially more random labels focused on the confident core (certification needs >= 45 labels per testable zone, and much more to hit alpha = 0.05 given this ~9-14% underlying error level), or (b) accepting a looser guarantee, e.g. alpha \u2248 0.14 would certify roughly the top 15-25% of the map. If you relabel, run the plan again through olmoearth_plan_label_sample and re-certify \u2014 happy to set that up.", "seq": 6, "t": 22.182, "seconds": 8.477}
